course: dictionary
lesson: 4803
title: Humming in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word, and ask what would fit. «The humming you hear in the kitchen is the compressor switching on.» A compressor is a machine, so humming here is a low, steady buzzing sound, not a tune.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The buzzing you hear in the kitchen is the compressor switching on» still makes sense, so humming means buzzing here. The clue «the quiet is it resting» also tells you that humming is the noise made while the machine is working.
explain: When someone hums a tune, they sing it with their lips closed, making a «mmm» sound. Look for the clue words: hum a tune and hum along are about singing, and the humming of bees is about a buzzing sound. Humming with activity is different again: it means busy.
fact: Humming can mean singing a tune with your lips closed, making a «mmm» sound.
fact: Humming can mean a low, steady buzzing sound, like bees, a fridge or a machine.
fact: As an adjective, humming can mean busy and full of activity, as in «humming with activity».
fact: «The humming noise is the compressor, a small pump, switching on and off to keep the inside cold.»
fact: Humming sounds are made by vibrations, which is why they are linked to how sound is made in science.
exercise: «The humming you hear in the kitchen is the compressor switching on.» What does humming mean here? | Singing a tune with closed lips | Dancing in a busy kitchen | A loud crash | *A low, steady buzzing sound
exercise: In music lessons, children hum a tune. What does hum a tune mean? | Stop singing and sit down | Play a tune on a drum | *Sing a tune with your lips closed | Write the words of a tune down
exercise: «Near your town, transformers in a humming substation turn the voltage down.» Find and copy one word that shows the substation is busy. | transformers | *humming | voltage | substation
test: «The humming of bees filled the garden on a warm summer day.» What does humming mean here? | A soft, sad song | Very quiet and still | Singing with closed lips | *A low, steady buzzing sound
test: Which sentence uses humming to mean busy? | She hummed a tune while she brushed her hair. | *The office was humming with activity all morning. | The fridge was humming quietly at night. | The bees hummed and then flew away.
exam: «A fridge is one of the few machines in a house that runs day and night.» Why does this help you work out what humming means in «the humming noise is the compressor»? | *It tells you the humming comes from a machine that is always working | It tells you the humming means the fridge is empty | It tells you the humming is a bird singing a song | It tells you the humming is a person laughing
